      "writtenOn": "2022-06-24T09:54:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that it\u0027s pretty unlikely that you\u0027ll go over 255 but I think it doesn\u0027t hurt to keep more room? The spec doesn\u0027t specify any max value and I checked what some other projects were doing but it\u0027s all over the place. I\u0027ve seen:\n\n8 + 8 + 8\n8 + 8 + 16\n32 + 16 + 16\n8 + 12 + 12\n12 + 10 + 12\n\nSome people also use base 10 digits (e.g. major*100*100 + minor*100 + patch). In this case I\u0027ve seen either 2 or 3 digits used.\n\n8+8+16 (total \u003d 32bits) might be a good compromise if you think 32+16+16 is overkill? Or 3 digits per element? In which case the max is 999999999 which also fits in a uint32_t",
      "parentUuid": "26d559b0_0661b8a7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
